---- MODULE MissionariesAndCannibals ----
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets

CONSTANTS Missionaries, Cannibals

ASSUME Missionaries \subseteq Nat /\ Cannibals \subseteq Nat
ASSUME Missionaries # {} /\ Cannibals # {}

\* Two river banks: east and west. The boat shuttles a group of size 1 or 2
\* across the river; it may never cross empty. No missionaries on a bank may
\* ever be outnumbered by cannibals, so the move is guarded by that safety
\* test before it is allowed to happen.
\* A solution trace is generated by a violation of the "east bank is empty"
\* invariant, so checking that invariant to global safety is the real goal.

Banks == {"east", "west"}
People == Missionaries \cup Cannibals

VARIABLES location, boat, boatBank

vars == <<location, boat, boatBank>>

\* Location is a per-bank roster; boatBank names the dock the boat currently
\* sits at; boat is the group in transit (empty when docked).
TypeOK ==
  /\ location \in [Banks -> SUBSET People]
  /\ boat \in SUBSET People
  /\ boatBank \in Banks

Init ==
  /\ location = [b \in Banks |-> IF b = "east" THEN People ELSE {}]
  /\ boat = {}
  /\ boatBank = "east"

\* A move both lifts a group off their bank and drops it on the far side, so
\* the safety test must be applied to the post-move rosters on both banks.
Move ==
  \E g \in SUBSET (location[boatBank]) :
    /\ g # {}
    /\ Cardinality(g) <= 2
    /\ \A b \in Banks :
         LET roster == (IF b = boatBank THEN location[b] \ g ELSE location[b])
                      \cup (IF b = (IF boatBank = "east" THEN "west" ELSE "east") THEN g ELSE {})
         IN (Missionaries \subseteq roster) \/ (Cardinality(remainder(cannibals, roster)) <= Cardinality(remainder(missionaries, roster)))
    /\ location' = [b \in Banks |->
                      (IF b = boatBank THEN location[b] \ g ELSE location[b])
                        \cup (IF b = (IF boatBank = "east" THEN "west" ELSE "east") THEN g ELSE {})]
    /\ boat' = g
    /\ boatBank' = (IF boatBank = "east" THEN "west" ELSE "east")

\* Once every person has crossed, the boat runs empty and the system rests.
Rest ==
  /\ \A b \in Banks : location[b] = {}
  /\ UNCHANGED vars

Next == Move \/ Rest

\* The invariant version: on every bank, missionaries are never outnumbered
\* by cannibals; the liveness version is the complement of the solved check.
Solution ==
  /\ \A b \in Banks :
       (Missionaries \subseteq location[b]) \/ (Cardinality(remainder(cannibals, location[b])) <= Cardinality(remainder(missionaries, location[b])))
  /\ boat # {}
  /\ Cardinality(boat) <= 2

Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars

\* The liveness property captured here is the complement of the solved check,
\* included so the model checks something nontrivial beyond the invariant.
\* The solution trace comes from an invariant violation, not this.
MissionariesNeverOutnumbered == (\A b \in Banks :
  (Missionaries \subseteq location[b]) \/ (Cardinality(remainder(cannibals, location[b])) <= Cardinality(remainder(missionaries, location[b]))))
====